---
/**
 * The videogame nav overlay — a d-pad in the instrument grammar. Four arrow
 * keycaps in a cross: up/down cycle CHANNEL, left/right cycle METRIC (BEAT
 * only). The keys light up on real key press (same press flash as the
 * command-bar chips) and are themselves clickable/tappable controls that
 * dispatch the matching arrow key. On non-BEAT channels the left/right pair
 * dims (inactive). It pulses once on page load to teach that keys work.
 *
 * It is UI, not decoration, so reduced motion keeps it — only its pulse and
 * press animations go static. On mobile it shrinks and reads as the swipe
 * affordance hint (still tappable).
 *
 * Persisted across channel switches; all behaviour lives in the layout's
 * single persistent controller (keydown flash, click dispatch, route dim,
 * load pulse), so nothing re-binds after a soft navigation.
 */
---

<div id="dpad" class="dpad" transition:persist="dpad" aria-label="Navigation d-pad">
  <div class="dpad-cross">
    <button class="dpad-key dpad-up" data-key="ArrowUp" aria-label="Previous channel">
      <span aria-hidden="true">▲</span>
    </button>
    <button class="dpad-key dpad-left" data-key="ArrowLeft" aria-label="Previous metric (beat channel)">
      <span aria-hidden="true">◀</span>
    </button>
    <span class="dpad-hub" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <button class="dpad-key dpad-right" data-key="ArrowRight" aria-label="Next metric (beat channel)">
      <span aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
    </button>
    <button class="dpad-key dpad-down" data-key="ArrowDown" aria-label="Next channel">
      <span aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
    </button>
  </div>
  <div class="dpad-legend" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="dpad-legend-h">◀▶ METRIC</span>
    <span class="dpad-legend-v">▲▼ CHANNEL</span>
    <span class="dpad-legend-swipe">SWIPE TO NAVIGATE</span>
  </div>
</div>
